--
GCC alignment semantics in C++: packed + aligned(n) is exactly n (alignof);
a struct containing an aligned class-template instance (directly, as an
array, via typedef/alias -- also when the member is the instance's first
use) is padded to its alignment; aligned(n) in a typedef/alias of a scalar
applies, on an alias of a class type it is ignored (as g++ does).
